From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: domicile CI <ci@domicile.invalid>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 00:39:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a monitor is named by its panel, not by an id

`display_id()` is already identity: EDID-derived, stable across a hotplug,
and different for two of the same monitor. What it cannot be is a NAME. It is
an int64 nobody can predict from looking at a desk, so writing "put the
left-hand monitor here" means first reading one off a log and then typing a
number that means nothing -- which is what a Domicile output profile had to
match on.

edid_name.{h,cc} builds the string kanshi and sway match on instead:
"<MAKE> <MODEL> <SERIAL>". Its one real piece of work is the serial, which is
the one part display::EdidParser does not keep -- it hashes it, deliberately,
because a browser should not carry an identifier around. That is the right
default there and the wrong one here: the serial is what tells three identical
U3219Qs apart, it is read off the user's own hardware, shown to the user, and
goes nowhere else.

Deliberately free of Chromium types, so the descriptor walk and the four ways
a name can be partly missing compile and run outside a Chromium tree.
drm_screen.cc puts what it builds on display::Display::label, which is the
field that exists for exactly this and which nothing on this platform was
setting.
---
 ui/ozone/platform/drm/BUILD.gn | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ui/ozone/platform/drm/BUILD.gn b/ui/ozone/platform/drm/BUILD.gn
index 07f08aab36..bc0be3c353 100644
--- a/ui/ozone/platform/drm/BUILD.gn
+++ b/ui/ozone/platform/drm/BUILD.gn
@@ -136,6 +136,8 @@ source_set("gbm") {
     "domicile/drm_screen.h",
     "domicile/drm_vt_switcher.cc",
     "domicile/drm_vt_switcher.h",
+    "domicile/edid_name.cc",
+    "domicile/edid_name.h",
     "host/drm_window_host_manager.h",
     "host/gpu_thread_adapter.h",
     "host/gpu_thread_observer.h",
@@ -259,6 +261,7 @@ source_set("gbm_unittests") {
     "domicile/drm_modeset_unittest.cc",
     "domicile/drm_screen_unittest.cc",
     "domicile/drm_vt_switcher_unittest.cc",
+    "domicile/edid_name_unittest.cc",
   ]
 
   # `ui/display/manager/test/fake_display_snapshot.h` is the one thing this
